to learn the syntax of the code  we can see the text inside the console  it has three lines the first one is a  comment so  we use a hash sign to comment out any  text or use it to annotate the code so  it's easier to read  then there are two lines these are used  to call a package by its name and assign  it with a name that will later be used  to call functions from the library  functions that the package contains  once the packages are loaded you can  hover over the small i icon to see which  packages have been actually loaded  to load the data set you need to create  an object any name can be used for  example you can use df or data frame or  any name like gene expression but  without the spaces or unusual characters  to view the data simply refer to the  object name and it will be printed out  in the console  once the data is loaded you can perform  many functions on different parts of the  data you can call a specific row column  or cell this will be extremely useful as  we prepare the data for analysis
 

